|\n| **1** | Partial match       | Only a small portion of the content is present, and it may not fully address the user's intent.                                                                    |\n| **0** | Off-Topic/Other     | Off-topic in comparison to ground truth and/or does not fit any of the above categories.                                                                           |\n\n## Instruction\nReturn the numeric score (0-5) and a concise justification for the score. Be as concise as possible, but make sure to include all relevant information.\n`;return on?`${on} ${qi}`:`# Compare the model submission to the ground truth response:\n\nYou need to evaluate the submission with respect to the ground truth response. Both the submission and the ground truth response are attempting to answer the same user question:\n\n- The ground truth response contains a minimal correct answer to the user's question, while the model submission is the response generated by the model in any format (text, JSON, visuals, etc)\n- Ensure you consider the meaning of the ground truth response when evaluating the model submission. Use of modifiers to enhance or change the meaning of information (e.g., "approximately", "more than", "less than", "around", "close to", "not", "as compared to" etc.) should be taken into account when assessing correctness.\n- The model submission may present information in text segments, visual elements, or both. Information might be split between visuals and text, so evaluate the complete narrative across all formats when evaluating correctness.\n- When information appears in visuals (charts, tables, etc.), it should be considered equivalent to having that information in text form.\n- Visual representations of data (e.g., charts showing a trend) should be considered equivalent to textual descriptions of the same trend.\n- The model submission may contain numbers that are less or more precise than the ground truth response, the model submission should still be considered correct, as long as the numbers are approximately equal. Keep in mind that the numbers may also be in a different format (e.g. 1,000 vs 1000) especially in the case of large numbers, have different representation (e.g, $1 Million vs $1000000), and may or may not mention units like celsius or $ or some other currency etc., between the ground truth and the model submission, but as long as the numbers are approximately equal, the model submission should still be considered correct.\n- The model submission may not mention an exact date or time concerning the information that is discussed in the ground truth response, but as long as the model submission contains the same information as the ground truth, the model submission should still be considered correct.\n- Information may be organized differently in the model submission, but the core facts and insights should align with the ground truth to be considered correct. ${qi}`}var Zo=function(Ze){return Ze.None="none",Ze.AddBasicAnnotation="addBasicAnnotation",Ze.AddAnnotationWithMetadata="addDetailedAnnotation",Ze.AddAnnotationAndHydrateChatContextWithMetadata="addAnnotationAndHydrateChatContextWithMetadata",Ze}(Zo||{}),eo=function(Ze){return Ze.Error="error",Ze.Info="info",Ze.Warning="warning",Ze}(eo||{}),Ao=function(Ze){return Ze.ZeroPrompt="zero-prompt",Ze.PromptMenu="prompt-menu",Ze}(Ao||{}),xt=function(Ze){return Ze.CreatePage="create-page",Ze.DataQuestion="data-question",Ze.General="general",Ze.Search="search",Ze.Summary="summary",Ze.VerifiedAnswer="verified-answer",Ze}(xt||{});const Qt={state:"loading"},Rt=!1,en=1,Ni=500,wt=1e4,Ri={hasValidatedArtifact:!1,isValidatingArtifact:!1,validationError:void 0,requiresArtifactValidation:!1};var Cn=function(Ze){return Ze[Ze.Sidecar=0]="Sidecar",Ze[Ze.Immersive=1]="Immersive",Ze[Ze.Inline=2]="Inline",Ze}(Cn||{})},451962:(le,F,e)=>{"use strict";e.d(F,{A_:()=>pr,Zt:()=>Qo,EW:()=>Li,OR:()=>eo,GA:()=>We,pX:()=>xn,it:()=>ir,TA:()=>Ut,Sd:()=>si,d4:()=>sc,JS:()